        question: "Can old timber floors carry apartments or offices?",
        answer: "Often yes, but it must be verified, not assumed. The engineer load-rates each timber member and the plank decking against the new occupancy's code-required loads. Where members fall short, reinforcement - sistering, flitch plates, or supplemental steel - brings them into compliance. A century of leaks or insect damage can reduce capacity locally, which is why the assessment includes hands-on inspection of every framing line.",
