        question: "Why do high-rise plumbing stacks need parallel vent stacks?",
        answer: "Because dozens of stories of falling wastewater entrain air and create pressure swings — positive pressure below the flow, suction above — that can siphon or blow out fixture trap seals, letting sewer gas into occupied spaces. The parallel vent stack gives displaced air a free path so pressures stay near atmospheric and every trap keeps its water seal.",
